    "created_at": "2022-02-28T17:13:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-28T17:13:01Z",
    "body": "If you're using ZSH, you should be able to check this with a few tests on your end. Try the following snippet in .zshrc:\r\n\r\n```\r\nautoload -U colors && colors\r\nPS1=\"%B%{$fg[green]%}%n%{$reset_color%}@%B%{$fg[cyan]%}%M %{$fg[yellow]%}%~ %{$reset_color%}%% %b\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat should create a basic bolded ZSH prompt with a `user@host path` format:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4605384/156027202-e6d0b438-4155-4116-a786-3382b423c7ba.png)\r\n\r\nIf Terminus displays this incorrectly, then we can say with some confidence that the issue is in Terminus or how Terminus interacts with ZSH (since there's no starship involved in that prompt)\r\n\r\nIf Terminus does display this correctly, then there's most likely some interaction between Terminus and the ANSI display system that we (starship) haven't accounted for.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
