    "updated_at": "2022-02-28T19:26:25Z",
    "body": "On further investigation, it appears that Terminus does the white background with black text when it cannot interpret an ANSI escape code used to format text. Here are four samples borrowed from [this post](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/4842424/list-of-ansi-color-escape-sequences) in both Terminus and WezTerm:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4605384/156045217-6e9db838-d22b-4cd8-aeaf-b178487769c9.png)\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4605384/156045239-6544d656-65d0-44ed-9e25-b3ef313fe630.png)\r\n\r\nOf these, the first three use 8-bit colors, and the last uses the standard 4-bit color schemes. None of them use the true color spectrum that starship uses to interpret hex codes.\r\n\r\nIn fact, it appears that the 256-color support in Terminus is currently *completely broken* on my system, as the following snippet is supposed to generate the 256-color spectrum, but instead generates white blocks, while it works fine in WezTerm:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4605384/156045889-c3eb4006-273b-4e07-853e-c39bf37f5f2c.png)\r\n",
